-- title:
--   Ordered sum count for three distinct elements
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be an abelian group. For pairwise distinct $a,b,c\in G$ and any $z\in G$, let $R_S(z)$ count ordered pairs in $S^2$ with sum $z$. Then
--
--   $$R_{\{a,b,c\}}(z)=\mathbf1_{2a=z}+\mathbf1_{2b=z}+\mathbf1_{2c=z}+2\mathbf1_{a+b=z}+2\mathbf1_{a+c=z}+2\mathbf1_{b+c=z}.$$
--
--   Coincidences among the six sums are counted with their full multiplicity.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, https://github.com/alexcour/couret-finite-verifications/blob/65b828d9ffd016ce2a1b05403f303fa5f948c10f/research/correspondants_20261013/lean/CayleyTwoColourAbelian.lean#L272-L299, lines 272–299; source file SHA-256 c9643d6e3a677d5a903623825d50a309d87175a21ace2b7ab56939d9189f13b1; theorem Couret.CayleyDoublet.abelianOrderedSquare_triple

